<title>UK: Guinness, Grandmet fall on LVMH move.</title>
<headline>Guinness, Grandmet fall on LVMH move.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Guinness Plc and Grand Metropolitan Plc fell sharply after French LVMH said it would buy all Guinness' interest in joint ventures.</p>
<p>This would give LVMH the right to continue marketing and distributing Guinness brands in key markets such as for example China, the U.S., France, Hong Kong and Japan for at least 10 years, the French firm said.</p>
<p>Guinness fell 9-1/2 pence to 587 pence, while Grandmet lost 9-1/2 to 586-1/2.</p>
</text>
